#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Fold the need-state segment map into dashboard.json (powers segments.html).

Segments are an AUTHORED CLASSIFICATION, not a field in the source data. Every SKU in the
PDI panel was assigned by a rule set over brand, PRODUCT_TYPE, SUB_PRODUCT_TYPE and the
product description. The ordering of those rules is deliberate: positioning beats
formulation, so Celsius and Bang land in Wellness and Fitness rather than Zero-Sugar even
though both are sugar-free. "Zero-Sugar Mainstream" therefore holds only the zero variants
of the classic brands, which is the need it actually represents.

Box area on the page is trailing-12-month revenue, so the treemap doubles as market share.

Field keys are short because this ships to the browser inside the aggregate:
  t12 = trailing-12-month revenue   top = leading brands [{b: brand, r: revenue}]
  prod = top SKUs [{b: brand, d: description, fl: flavour, sz: unit size,
                    r: T12M revenue, st: stores stocking it}]

Idempotent - re-running overwrites only the `segments` key. Run after build_dashboard_json.py.
"""
import json
import os

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))))
OUT = os.path.join(ROOT, "public", "data", "dashboard.json")

